UHFFFAOYSA-M\nL232: \nL233: Description\nL234: ### Application\nL235: \nL236: Sodium phosphate monobasic dihydrate has been used for preparing phosphate buffer solution. It has also been used as a mobile phase for high-performance liquid chromatography.\nL237: ### Biochem/physiol Actions\nL238: \nL239: Sodium phosphate monobasic also referred to as sodium dihydrogen phosphate is a chemical reagent possesses high buffering capacity and is used for preparing biological buffers. It was used as a phosphate supplement for determining whether phosphate supplementation can prevent rickets in very low birth weight infants with prenatal deficiency of phosphate.\nL240: \nL241: * * *\nL242: \nL243: ## Compare Similar Items\nL244: \nL245: 【16†View Full Comparison】\nL246: \nL247: * * *\nL248: \nL249: Show Differences\nL250: \nL251: [Input]\nL252: \nL253: 1 of 1\nL254: ###### This Item\nL255:  | 71505  | 71500  | 04243\nL256: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL257: 【17†Sigma-Aldrich 04269 Sodium phosphate monobasic dihydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【18†Sigma-Aldrich 71505 Sodium phosphate monobasic dihydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【19†Sigma-Aldrich 71500 Sodium phosphate monobasic dihydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich 04243 Potassium phosphate monobasic】[Button: Quick View]\nL258: description meets analytical specification of Ph. Eur., BP, USP, 98-100.5% (calc. to the dried substance)  | description BioUltra, Molecular Biology, ≥99.0% (T)  | description purum p.a., crystallized, ≥99.0% (T)  | description meets analytical specification of Ph. Eur., NF, anhydrous, 98-100.5% (calc. to the dried substance)\nL259: form powder or crystals  | form powder or crystals  | form crystals  | form crystalline\nL260: assay 98-100.5% (calc. to the dried substance)  | assay≥99.0% (T)  | assay≥99.0% (T)  | assay 98-100.5% (calc. to the dried substance)\nL261: Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 300  | Quality Level 200\nL262: anion traces chloride (Cl^{-}): ≤50 mg/kg, sulfa